      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That exhaustion is real—grief can drain you until even existing feels like a chore. You don't have to fight it all at once; let yourself rest in the gray for a while, without pressure to feel anything more. The weight may not lift today, but you don't have to carry it alone—let someone sit beside you in that dark room, even in silence. One breath, one hour at a time.",
      "source": "target",
